## Summary

**Implemented** `crates/application/src/install.rs` — the §8.3 install planner:

- **Re-exports** `InstallPlan`, `StorageDestination`, `TransferMode`, `VerificationPlan` from `ports::transfer` (the architecture-spec types are already owned there; duplicating them would violate "transcribe exactly").
- **`SignaturePolicy`** enum (`Required`/`Optional`, snake_case serde) — encodes the "policy requires a signature" branch.
- **`InstallPlanRequest`** DTO — every async fact the planner needs (catalog entry, destination, free bytes, source size, source range support, desired mode, signature policy, replaces/retained version IDs, retained LKG bytes). Caller gathers these from `CatalogSource`, `TransferSource`, and `PlatformAdapter`; the planner performs no I/O.
- **`InstallPlanError`** — one variant per §8.3 failure, in spec order: `DestinationNotWritable`, `FinalBytesDoNotFit`, `TemporaryAndRetainedDoNotFit`, `NoVerifiedDigest`, `SignatureRequiredButMissing`, `RangeStrategyIncompatible`.
- **`plan_install(request) -> Result<InstallPlan, InstallPlanError>`** — pure synchronous function. Computes `download_bytes` (0 for `LocalCopy`, else `source_size_bytes`), `temporary_bytes = download_bytes`, `final_bytes = artifact_size_bytes`, `free_bytes_after = free_bytes_before - final_bytes` (conservative; A-04 keeps LKG readable through activation). Trust check uses the `"verified"` token that `catalog-openzim` writes. `zim_structure_check` is always true (catalog entries are ZIM artifacts).
- **No new dependencies** — `Cargo.toml` already had `serde` and `thiserror`.

**`cargo check -p application` result:** fails on 12 errors, **all** in `crates/ports/src/platform.rs` (referenced-but-undefined `PlatformError`, `PlatformStorageRoot`, `PlatformCapabilityReport`, `PowerState`, `NetworkState`) — that's the platform-port coder's incomplete file, not mine. My `install.rs` produces no errors of its own and every type/field it references is verified present in `ports::transfer` and `ports::catalog`.
